Commercial guidance introduced in 0.4.0 adapts Revenue-Centric Design, based
on Richard's (@richardrx) work. Those additions are subject to the full
source-available terms in licenses/revenue-centric-design.txt.

Those terms require attribution, preservation of the full license, and exclude
betting, casino, gambling and the real-money gaming/loot-box applications named
there. The commercial additions are not offered under CC BY 4.0 alone. See
SOURCES.md for the files and integration passages covered.
The shared offer brief in 0.25.0 adapts ideas from Corey Haines' MIT-licensed
product-marketing skill, mbfinotti's MIT-licensed sales-skills (ICP definition
and deal value) and Anthropic's Apache-2.0 knowledge-work-plugins create-an-asset
skill. Retain the upstream notices in:
licenses/coreyhaines-marketingskills.txt
licenses/mbfinotti-sales-skills.txt
licenses/anthropic-knowledge-work-plugins.txt
The Apache-2.0 material was changed: rewritten in this skill's own words and
reduced to the rules named in SOURCES.md.
